# Specimen taxonomy

Sources of truth:

- Facets / free-tag rules → [`src/specimens/taxonomy.ts`](src/specimens/taxonomy.ts)
- Inspiration directory → [`src/specimens/inspiration.ts`](src/specimens/inspiration.ts)
- Human mirror → [`docs/inspiration-directory.md`](docs/inspiration-directory.md)

Every specimen **must** set `facets`. Optionally set `inspiredBy` and freeform `tags`.

## Facets (required)

| Facet | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `kind` | `overlay` · `transition` · `loop` · `interaction` |
| `tech` | `css-only` · `tiny-js` |
| `scope` | `card` · `fullscreen` · `inline` |
| `intensity` | `subtle` · `graphic` · `maximal` |

## Inspiration (optional, preferred for game lineage)

```ts
inspiredBy: {
  franchise: 'persona',      // category — Persona, Zelda, …
  works: ['persona-5'],      // optional specific titles
}
```

- Franchise = category chip (e.g. **Persona**)
- Works = specific labels (e.g. **Persona 5**)
- Omit `works` when the language is franchise-wide
- **Never** put franchise/work ids (or “persona-inspired”) in `tags` — use `inspiredBy`
- Adding a game: extend `INSPIRATION_DIRECTORY` + update `docs/inspiration-directory.md` in the same change

## Free tags (effect flavor)

Kebab-case, short, specific: `marquee`, `comic`, `wipe`, `glitch`.  
Suggested list: `SUGGESTED_FREE_TAGS` in `inspiration.ts`.  
Do not repeat facet values or inspiration ids.

## Assignment rules

- `tech: 'css-only'` ↔ no `demo.js` / no `files.js`; `tech: 'tiny-js'` ↔ JS present
- Extending facet vocab → edit `taxonomy.ts`, `spec-check.mjs`, and this rule together
- Extending inspiration → edit `inspiration.ts`, docs mirror, this rule if semantics change

Catalogue: facet AND filters + Inspiration/Title chips; plates show facets → inspiredBy → tags. See `55_catalogue`.
